    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9572" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">compĕrendĭnātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		comperendino, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a deferring of the time</i> (<i>of
				trial</i>) <i>to the third day</i> or <i>later</i> (post-Aug.), <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep.
				97, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep. 5, 21, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 2, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 14,
				2, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. Or. 38</span></i>; cf.
				<i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 1, 9, §
			26</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, in gen., <i>delay</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sine ullā comperendinatione,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ambros. in Luc. 1, 8</span></i>
			.</div>
